{
  "abstract": "For two finite classical–quantum states, the absolute change in conditional subentropy is bounded by their joint trace distance times the average of κ along the line segment joining their quantum marginals. For distinct states the change is strictly smaller than their joint trace distance. Nevertheless, one is the optimal global Lipschitz constant for every fixed number of labels n ≥ 2 and every quantum dimension m ≥ 1. For n ≥ 2 and any prescribed quantum marginal τ, the optimal constant is κ(τ), the operator norm of the matrix K(τ) in equation (27).",
